  "notes": "Synagogue / public building, all warm sandstone ashlar (block coursing not expressible). Two flat-roofed blocks: wider left block (3 floors, stepped sand-coloured cornice) and a right stair tower whose parapet steps HIGHER than the main block (schema has no per-volume extra parapet height -- expressed via taller fascia). A full-height vertical GLASS-BLOCK strip (#8a8c79) joins the two blocks, modelled here as per-floor narrow bands with style 'glassblock' (factory extension needed; bands are horizontal by design). ALL windows have grey security bars/grilles -- no bars field in openings, factory extension needed. Floor 1 of the main block has a curved balcony at x~0.28 with cream metal railing and a chunky wood-trimmed (#be7d49) door surround; the terraces entry cannot encode floor/position/curvature. Ground floor: raised entry porch/terrace with cream bar railings, a straight stair flight (right) and a long accessibility RAMP with handrails (left) -- none expressible, factory needs porch/stair/ramp prims. Below plaza level the tower has two semi-basement garage doors (split-level not expressible). Colourful recycling bins (magenta/yellow/cyan/orange panels) stand at the tower base -- prop factory pending. Frontage is an OPEN pinkish stone-slab plaza straight to the street (no fence despite spec's metal fence -- the restyle shows none), lawn and low-poly trees visible at the left horizon, no road in frame (road block omitted). Sampled colours from 12x9 grids 2026-07-03."
